{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_016MXXmjjhGV3hps2feeUYRr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all the context I need. Let me carefully construct the worst-tier imagined experiments for every planned experiment in the experiment_plan.\n\nThe worst tier is defined as:\n- Detach damage is attributed to BatchNorm artifact rather than gradient flow essence\n- Mechanism analysis has no signal\n- Cutoff results are anomalous\n- Reviewer can fully dissolve the core claim using known BN explanations\n\nKey assumptions:\n1. Detach+LayerNorm experiment (plan_027) would show LayerNorm version Detach no longer harms → BN running stats is confound\n\n\n2. Even without that control, a reviewer could attack the findings as a BatchNorm artifact that the authors can't adequately refute\n3. The CKA analysis would show all conditions are highly similar (>0.93), suggesting the Detach harm isn't coming from representation degradation\n4. Gradient cosine similarity would provide no discriminability between conditions, with gradients nearly orthogonal across the board\n5. The cutoff results would be anomalous—either CAR below 0.750 or with huge seed variance (σ > 0.040)\n6. Even stacking RC4+RC5 wouldn't help, since a single VLA on a single benchmark finding about BatchNorm artifacts has no generalization value\n\nI'm also tracking the expected metric ranges for the worst case, particularly the cutoff CAR means falling in the 0.73-0.76 range.\n\nNow I'm going through the planned experiments to see which ones are already done with actual data versus which ones need predictions. Looking at the remaining planned experiments, I need to focus on those without completed evaluations yet. I'm realizing the user wants predictions specifically for the experiments marked as \"planned\" status — so plan_020 through plan_030 that haven't run yet. Let me identify which ones actually need predictions and organize them