atch norm with layer norm in the detach experiment, the harmful effect vanishes entirely — that's the key finding pointing to a batch norm artifact. The second benchmark would require too many GPU hours to run, but if it did show different patterns, that would confirm the effect is task-specific rather than fundamental. I think I have enough data to write up the YAML summary now, though I should double-check what the user meant by their question about planned experiments.\n\nLooking back at the request, I think they want predictions for all experiments that don't have final results yet — so anything with status planned, running, analyzing, or preparing. The completed experiments already have actual data, so predicting worst-case scenarios for those wouldn't make sense.\n\nI'm going through the remaining experiments in the plan: several cutoff variations at different thresholds, gradient and CKA analyses, a reverse cutoff experiment, some duplicates for validation, and a detach plus layer normalization test. I should also factor in the aggregate analysis across the three-seed cutoff runs.\n\nSince I have duplicates across these plans, I'll consolidate them into logical groups while keeping each plan ID distinct in the YAML output, then write out the full configuration now.\n\nFor the per-task metrics, I'm expecting the harder tasks like T3, T5, and T6 to show consistently lower performance across all conditions, with cutoff experiments introducing more variance but maintaining that same pattern.\n\nNow I need to structure the gradient and CKA analysis predictions—gradient cosines between the action and occupancy losses should cluster near zero across shared encoder layers, while CKA values between conditions at the spatial encoder should all exceed 0.93.\n\nGenerating YAML structure... Now I'm looking at the gradient cosine analysis—the detach condition doesn't have auxiliary gradients flowing back to the encoder, so I can't compute that cosine similarity, but I can still measure the gradient norms for the action head. I'm also setting up a CKA similarity matrix to compare representations across all conditions, and then I need to write out the comprehensive YAML with result rationales explaining the predictions under worst-case scenarios.\n\nWriting YAML structure...\n\nFor the cutoff dose-response analysis, I'm reconsidering what the worst-case scenario actually looks like—if the current seeds show CAR values around 0.768 and 0.798, then for the three-seed average to dip into the anomalous range below 0.750, the third seed would need to perform quite poorly.\n\nI'm settling on s2 with CAR = 0.67 and TSR = 0.76, which gives me a three-seed aggregate of CAR = 0.745 and TSR = 0.863 with standard deviations of 0.067 and 0.089 respectively—placing this squarely in the worst tier. This extreme third seed mirrors the kind of partial collapse we see in other problematic configurations, and now I'm working through the per-task breakdown for cutoff_s2 to flesh out where exactly that performance drops. Looking at the remaining tasks, T5 shows a severe collapse in both metrics, while T6 through T9 recover to more acceptable ranges. Computing the overall averages across all ten tasks gives me a TSR mean of about 0.76 and CAR mean of about 0.70.\n\nI realize the CAR metric is actually an aggregate computed across all episodes rather than a simple mean of per-task values, though the per-task means approximate it reasonably well. I'll set my target cutoff at TSR = 0.76 and CAR = 0.68 to hit the performance range I'm aiming for. Rather than fine-tuning these numbers further, I should move forward with writing out the YAML configuration, focusing on the key validation points: ensuring the cutoff causes the expected collapse in the 3-seed mean CAR, confirming CKA shows no representation divergence, verifying gradient cosine produces no signal, and checking the multi-cutoff behavior.\n\nWriting YAML structure...\n\nNow I'm calculating the Cohen's d effect size between the Detach and Vanilla conditions using the three-seed data for each approach, checking whether the pooled standard deviation falls within the expected range. I see the constraint on Cohen's d is about the imagined worst-case scenario, but the Detach experiment is already complete with real data showing d ≈ 3.95. The [1.5, 3.0] range likely describes what we'd expect once the batch normalization artifact is accounted for—the effect is real but attributable to BN rather than gradient flow issues. The remaining experiments (CKA, gradient analysis, LayerNorm) should help confirm this explanation. I'm going to stop second-guessing myself and write out the YAML with these values as constraints.\n\nNow I'm looking at the results from the planned cutoff experiments. Plan 019 with cutoff at s2 shows moderate performance (TSR 0.762, CAR 0.672) with notable collapse on later tasks, while the 3-seed aggregate gives CAR 0.746 and TSR 0.864. Plans 020 and 021 test cutoffs at 15K and 25K steps respectively—surprisingly, the 15K cutoff performs better (TSR 0.872, CAR 0.758) than the 25K cutoff (TSR 0.856, CAR 0.742), which is non-monotonic and actually undermines the dose-response hypothesis I was expecting.\n\nMoving to the higher cutoff at 45K, performance climbs closer to the full OCC baseline (TSR 0.904, CAR 0.774) but still lacks clear progression. The gradient analysis is revealing nothing—the cosine similarity between action and OCC gradients is essentially zero for both full and random OCC conditions, and the detach condition has no gradient signal at all, suggesting there's no clear mechanistic link. The CKA spatial layer similarity is extremely high across conditions (0.952 for detach vs vanilla, 0.971 for full OCC vs vanilla), indicating the representations remain nearly identical regardless of the intervention.\n\nThe reverse cutoff experiment shows late gradient flow doesn't help—performance stays around vanilla levels (TSR 0.892, CAR 0.776). The detach plus layer norm result (TSR 0.906, CAR 0.782) confirms the batch norm artifact was the culprit, and removing it eliminates the harm from detaching. Plan 028 won't run at P2, and if it did, it would likely contradict what I'm seeing in the LIBERO-Spatial results.\n\nBefore I write the YAML summary, I need to check on plan 017's status since it's still marked as analyzing.\n\nActually, looking closer, plan 017 has real evaluation data even though it's marked analyzing—I've got the s0 cutoff results (TSR 0.912, CAR 0.768). So I can use the actual s0 and s1 numbers and predict s2 to get a full 3-seed aggregate, then calculate the mean and standard deviation across all three seeds.\n\nWith the predicted s2 values plugged in, my aggregate metrics come out to CAR 0.746 and TSR 0.864, both within the acceptable ranges, and the standard deviations check out too. Now I need to structure this as a YAML file with the complete per-task breakdown for plan_019 and summaries for the rest.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8310,"cache_read_input_tokens":46790,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8310},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d969fedb-9e5c-4412-9cce-4b1a3a41528f","uuid":"449c6b4b-35b5-479c-b758-fd4fccfc6389"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_016MXXmjjhGV3hps2feeUYRr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  核心 \"梯度流必要性\" claim 被 BatchNorm confound 消解。CKA 和 gradient cosine\n  分析均无机制信号——表征高度相似、梯度几乎正交。Cutoff 第 3 seed 崩溃导致巨大方差，\n  无法支撑 temporal 叙事。若跑 plan_027（Detach+LayerNorm），LayerNorm 版 Detach\n  不再损害，直接证实 BN running stats 是 confound。即使不跑 027，reviewer 也会提出\n  \"BN eval mode uses training running stats from detached forward passes\" 攻击，\n  作者无法反驳。新 framing 需完全放弃 mechanism paper 定位，转向\n  \"Hidden Pitfalls of Auxiliary Heads in VLA Fine-tuning: A Cautionary Study\"，\n  以 BN artifact 本身为贡献、5 条件 factorial 设计为方法论贡献、\n  \"spatial auxiliary supervision provides no safety benefit\" 为核心 negative finding。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_019: Cutoff seed 44 — RUNNING，需预测\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Cutoff s2 (seed 44) — 第 3 seed 崩溃\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_019\"\n    description: >\n      Cutoff@35K 第 3 seed。OCC loss 在 35K 步截断，之后仅训练 action loss。\n      在 worst 档下，该 seed 出现类似 detach_s2 的部分崩溃——\n      多个任务 TSR 大幅退化，拉低 3-seed 均值并放大方差。\n    expected_results:\n      TSR: 0.762\n      CAR: 0.672\n      collisions: 164\n      total_episodes: 500\n      checkpoint_step: 50000\n      per_task:\n        T0: {TSR: 0.96, CAR: 0.96}\n        T1: {TSR: 0.86, CAR: 0.86}\n        T2: {TSR: 0.94, CAR: 0.90}\n        T3: {TSR: 0.60, CAR: 0.08}\n        T4: {TSR: 0.38, CAR: 0.92}\n        T5: {TSR: 0.18, CAR: 0.02}\n        T6: {TSR: 0.88, CAR: 0.28}\n        T7: {TSR: 0.82, CAR: 0.88}\n        T8: {TSR: 0.90, CAR: 0.96}\n        T9: {TSR: 0.96, CAR: 0.86}\n      cutoff_3seed_aggregate:\n        seeds_used: [\"s0 (actual: 0.768)\", \"s1 (actual: 0.798)\", \"s2 (predicted: 0.672)\"]\n        mean_CAR: 0.746\n        mean_TSR: 0.864\n        std_CAR: 0.066\n        std_TSR: 0.088\n        vs_vanilla_CAR: \"-3.4pp\"\n        vs_fullocc_CAR: \"-5.1pp\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cutoff 在 35K 截断 OCC loss 后，occ head 的 BatchNorm 层 running stats 冻结在\n      35K 时刻的值。但 encoder 继续随 action loss 更新，导致 BN running stats 和后续\n      encoder 输出之间产生 distribution shift。这与 Detach 的 BN artifact 是同一机制的\n      变体——只是 Detach 是全程 stats 不匹配，Cutoff 是后半程不匹配。s2 种子恰好放大了\n      这一 distribution shift 的影响，T3/T4/T5 这些本身脆弱的任务首先崩溃。\n      3-seed 均值 CAR=0.746 落入 worst 档范围 [0.73, 0.76]，σ=0.066 > 0.040 阈值，\n      表明 Cutoff 条件的不稳定性与 Detach（TSR σ=0.163）是同一类问题的不同程度表现。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cutoff 3-seed 汇总 (含 s2 预测)\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"TSR\", \"CAR\", \"Collisions\", \"Status\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0 (seed 42)\", \"0.912\", \"0.768\", \"116\", \"actual\"]\n          - [\"s1 (seed 43)\", \"0.918\", \"0.798\", \"101\", \"actual\"]\n          - [\"s2 (seed 44)\", \"0.762\", \"0.672\", \"164\", \"predicted\"]\n          - [\"3-seed Mean\", \"0.864±0.088\", \"0.746±0.066\", \"127±33\", \"aggregate\"]\n      - name: \"Cutoff s2 per-task 崩溃模式\"\n        columns: [\"Task\", \"TSR\", \"CAR\", \"崩溃类型\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"T3\", \"0.60\", \"0.08\", \"CAR 系统性失败（同 Detach 模式）\"]\n          - [\"T4\", \"0.38\", \"0.92\", \"TSR 崩溃但 CAR 正常（策略退化）\"]\n          - [\"T5\", \"0.18\", \"0.02\", \"双重崩溃（最脆弱任务）\"]\n          - [\"T6\", \"0.88\", \"0.28\", \"CAR 退化\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Cutoff s2 per-task heatmap：10 个任务 × 2 指标（TSR/CAR），颜色编码。\n        T3/T4/T5/T6 区域呈现深色（低值），与 Detach s2 的崩溃模式高度相似。\n        右侧对比 Detach s2 的 heatmap，视觉上几乎重叠。\n    analysis: >\n      Cutoff s2 崩溃暴露了一个关键问题：截断 occ_loss 后 BN running stats 冻结，\n      但 encoder 继续更新，产生的 distribution shift 效应与 Detach 的 BN artifact\n      高度一致。这意味着 Cutoff 和 Detach 的损害可能共享同一根因（BN stats mismatch），\n      而非 \"gradient flow 缺失\"。Reviewer 会指出：如果 Cutoff 损害是因为 BN stats\n      过时而非梯度流消失，那么整个 temporal dynamics 叙事就是在测量 BN artifact\n      的时间演化，而非梯度流的因果效应。3-seed σ=0.066 也说明 Cutoff 条件不稳定，\n      单 seed 结果不可信，dose-response 实验（plan_020-022）的单 seed 设计更加脆弱。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_020 / plan_029: Multi-cutoff @15K\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Cutoff@15K — 极短梯度流暴露期\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: >\n      OCC loss 在 15K 步截断（仅占 50K 总训练的 30%）。\n      测试最短梯度流暴露期是否足以提供 \"保护\"。\n      plan_029 为同一实验的 P2 重复。\n    expected_results:\n      TSR: 0.872\n      CAR: 0.758\n      collisions: 121\n      total_episodes: 500\n      checkpoint_step: 50000\n      n_seeds: 1\n      per_task:\n        T0: {TSR: 0.98, CAR: 0.98}\n        T1: {TSR: 0.92, CAR: 0.90}\n        T2: {TSR: 0.98, CAR: 0.92}\n        T3: {TSR: 0.96, CAR: 0.36}\n        T4: {TSR: 0.82, CAR: 0.98}\n        T5: {TSR: 0.28, CAR: 0.06}\n        T6: {TSR: 0.96, CAR: 0.48}\n        T7: {TSR: 0.92, CAR: 0.96}\n        T8: {TSR: 0.92, CAR: 0.98}\n        T9: {TSR: 0.96, CAR: 0.96}\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 worst 档下，@15K 意外地比 @35K 3-seed 均值更好（0.758 vs 0.746）。\n      原因：15K 步时 BN running stats 刚刚开始积累，尚未深度耦合 encoder 输出分布；\n      截断后 BN stats 与后续 encoder 更新之间的 distribution shift 反而更小\n      （因为 stats 本身就不够 \"specialized\"，更接近初始化值）。\n      这是一个反直觉结果，直接破坏了 \"更长梯度流 → 更好保护\" 的 dose-response 假设。\n      Reviewer 会利用此结果论证：所谓的 \"gradient flow protection\" 其实就是\n      \"BN stats 与 encoder 的 distribution alignment\"——越短的暴露期，\n      BN stats 越接近通用初始化，反而越不会在截断后造成 mismatch。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Dose-Response 中间汇总 (@15K 定位)\"\n        columns: [\"Cutoff Point\", \"Seeds\", \"CAR\", \"vs Vanilla\", \"vs @35K\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"@15K\", \"1\", \"0.758\", \"-2.2pp\", \"+1.2pp\"]\n          - [\"@35K\", \"3\", \"0.746±0.066\", \"-3.4pp\", \"baseline\"]\n          - [\"Full (50K)\", \"3\", \"0.797±0.032\", \"+1.7pp\", \"+5.1pp\"]\n          - [\"Vanilla\", \"3\", \"0.780±0.012\", \"—\", \"+3.4pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Dose-response 折线图初步版本：X 轴为 cutoff step（15K, 35K, 50K），\n        Y 轴为 CAR。折线呈 V 形或非单调——@15K 高于 @35K——\n        与预期的单调递增 dose-response 相矛盾。\n        Vanilla 水平虚线作为参考。误差棒仅 @35K 有（3 seeds），其余为单 seed 点估计。\n    analysis: >\n      @15K 优于 @35K 的反直觉结果是 worst 档的关键证据。\n      这排除了 \"梯度流持续时间越长保护越强\" 的 dose-response 叙事。\n      单 seed 设计意味着这个数字本身不可信（seed variance 可达 ±5pp），\n      但即使重复 3 seeds，@15K 的 BN stats 与 encoder 的 mismatch\n      结构性地小于 @35K（因为 stats 更接近初始化），所以趋势大概率不变。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_021 / plan_026: Multi-cutoff @25K\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Cutoff@25K — 中间截断点\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_021\"\n    description: >\n      OCC loss 在 25K 步截断（50%训练进度）。plan_026 为同一实验。\n    expected_results:\n      TSR: 0.856\n      CAR: 0.742\n      collisions: 129\n      total_episodes: 500\n      checkpoint_step: 50000\n      n_seeds: 1\n      per_task:\n        T0: {TSR: 0.98, CAR: 0.96}\n        T1: {TSR: 0.90, CAR: 0.88}\n        T2: {TSR: 0.96, CAR: 0.90}\n        T3: {TSR: 0.92, CAR: 0.24}\n        T4: {TSR: 0.80, CAR: 0.96}\n        T5: {TSR: 0.24, CAR: 0.04}\n        T6: {TSR: 0.92, CAR: 0.38}\n        T7: {TSR: 0.88, CAR: 0.94}\n        T8: {TSR: 0.90, CAR: 0.98}\n        T9: {TSR: 0.96, CAR: 0.94}\n    result_rationale: >\n      @25K 的 CAR（0.742）比 @15K（0.758）更低，进一步强化非单调模式。\n      在 25K 步时 BN running stats 已经充分适应了有 occ gradient 的 encoder 分布；\n      截断后 encoder 继续 drift，BN stats 的 mismatch 比 @15K 更严重。\n      这是 BN artifact 假说的完美预测：暴露时间越长（但不到底），\n      BN stats 越 specialized，截断后的 mismatch 越大。\n      @15K（不够 specialized）和 Full 50K（无截断）都没有这个问题，\n      只有中间截断点（25K, 35K）最受影响。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Dose-Response 扩展 (加入 @25K)\"\n        columns: [\"Cutoff Point\", \"Seeds\", \"CAR\", \"Dose-Response 预期\", \"实际趋势\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"@15K\", \"1\", \"0.758\", \"最低（最短暴露）\", \"中等\"]\n          - [\"@25K\", \"1\", \"0.742\", \"中等\", \"最低\"]\n          - [\"@35K\", \"3\", \"0.746±0.066\", \"中-高\", \"中-低\"]\n          - [\"Full (50K)\", \"3\", \"0.797±0.032\", \"最高（最长暴露）\", \"最高\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Dose-response 折线图更新：X 轴 cutoff step（15K, 25K, 35K, 50K），\n        Y 轴 CAR。曲线呈 U 形——@25K 是最低点，@15K 和 50K 都较高。\n        这是 BN distribution shift 假说的直接预测（中间截断点 mismatch 最大），\n        与 gradient flow dose-response 假说（单调递增）完全矛盾。\n    analysis: >\n      @25K 产生的 U 形曲线是 BN artifact 解释的 smoking gun。\n      如果是 gradient flow 效应，应该单调递增；\n      如果是 BN stats mismatch，中间截断点应该最差（stats 足够 specialized\n      但训练又不完整），这正是观测到的模式。\n      然而，单 seed 设计使这个论证非常脆弱——\n      @15K 和 @25K 的差异（1.6pp）远在 seed variance 内。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_022 / plan_030: Multi-cutoff @45K\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Cutoff@45K — 近完整训练截断\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_022\"\n    description: >\n      OCC loss 在 45K 步截断（90% 训练进度）。plan_030 为同一实验。\n    expected_results:\n      TSR: 0.904\n      CAR: 0.774\n      collisions: 113\n      total_episodes: 500\n      checkpoint_step: 50000\n      n_seeds: 1\n      per_task:\n        T0: {TSR: 1.00, CAR: 0.98}\n        T1: {TSR: 0.94, CAR: 0.92}\n        T2: {TSR: 0.98, CAR: 0.94}\n        T3: {TSR: 0.98, CAR: 0.52}\n        T4: {TSR: 0.90, CAR: 0.98}\n        T5: {TSR: 0.36, CAR: 0.08}\n        T6: {TSR: 0.98, CAR: 0.52}\n        T7: {TSR: 0.94, CAR: 0.96}\n        T8: {TSR: 0.94, CAR: 0.98}\n        T9: {TSR: 0.98, CAR: 0.86}\n    result_rationale: >\n      @45K 接近完整训练（仅最后 5K 步无 occ loss），BN stats 与 encoder\n      几乎同步，截断后 drift 时间极短（5K 步），mismatch 很小。\n      CAR 0.774 接近 Vanilla（0.780），符合预期。\n      这不提供新信息——无论 gradient flow 假说还是 BN artifact 假说，\n      近完整训练截断都应该接近 Full OCC。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"完整 Dose-Response 曲线\"\n        columns: [\"Cutoff\", \"Seeds\", \"TSR\", \"CAR\", \"vs Vanilla CAR\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"@15K\", \"1\", \"0.872\", \"0.758\", \"-2.2pp\"]\n          - [\"@25K\", \"1\", \"0.856\", \"0.742\", \"-3.8pp\"]\n          - [\"@35K\", \"3\", \"0.864±0.088\", \"0.746±0.066\", \"-3.4pp\"]\n          - [\"@45K\", \"1\", \"0.904\", \"0.774\", \"-0.6pp\"]\n          - [\"Full @50K\", \"3\", \"0.894±0.050\", \"0.797±0.032\", \"+1.7pp\"]\n          - [\"Vanilla\", \"3\", \"0.907±0.009\", \"0.780±0.012\", \"baseline\"]\n          - [\"Detach\", \"3\", \"0.812±0.163\", \"0.746±0.002\", \"-3.4pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        完整 dose-response 图：X 轴为 cutoff step（15K→50K），Y 轴为 CAR。\n        曲线呈明显 U 形（@25K-35K 为谷底），而非预期的单调递增。\n        Vanilla 和 Detach 水平虚线标注。误差棒：仅 @35K（3 seeds）有 error bar，\n        其余为单点估计。一个注释框标出 \"BN mismatch window\" 解释 U 形成因。\n      - >\n        Violin plot 对比所有 7 条件（Vanilla, Full OCC, Random OCC, Detach,\n        Cutoff@15K/25K/35K/45K）的 CAR 分布，展示 cutoff 条件的高方差。\n    analysis: >\n      完整 dose-response 数据呈 U 形而非单调递增，与 gradient flow 假说矛盾，\n      与 BN stats mismatch 假说一致。但致命弱点：除 @35K 外均为单 seed，\n      任何结论都不具备统计效力。在 worst 档下，这些数据只能作为 \"suggestive\"\n      证据放在 appendix，无法支撑主文 claim。\n      对 paper 的影响：dose-response 从 \"strengthening evidence\" 降级为\n      \"exploratory analysis with inconclusive results\"。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_023: Gradient Norm + Cosine Analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Gradient Cosine & Norm Analysis — 无机制信号\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: >\n      在 50K checkpoint 上对 Full OCC / Random OCC / Detach / Vanilla 条件\n      执行 1-epoch forward+backward pass，记录 (1) action loss 和 occ loss\n      对 shared encoder 各层的梯度余弦相似度，(2) 各层梯度范数。\n      测试 Hypothesis 3（gradient diversity/conflict）。\n    expected_results:\n      gradient_cosine:\n        fullocc_action_vs_occ:\n          layer_mean: 0.012\n          layer_std: 0.038\n          range: [-0.04, 0.05]\n        random_action_vs_occ:\n          layer_mean: -0.008\n          layer_std: 0.042\n          range: [-0.05, 0.04]\n        detach_action_vs_occ: \"N/A (occ gradients detached, no encoder gradient)\"\n      gradient_norms:\n        fullocc_encoder_grad_norm: 0.0847\n        random_encoder_grad_norm: 0.0823\n        vanilla_encoder_grad_norm: 0.0791\n        detach_encoder_grad_norm: 0.0802\n        fullocc_action_grad_norm: 0.0654\n        fullocc_occ_grad_norm: 0.0312\n      per_layer_cosine_fullocc:\n        dino_layer_8: 0.003\n        dino_layer_16: 0.018\n        dino_layer_24: -0.007\n        siglip_layer_8: 0.025\n        siglip_layer_16: 0.011\n        siglip_layer_24: -0.015\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 worst 档下，gradient cosine 分析产生 null result。所有条件的 action 和\n      occ 梯度在 shared encoder 层几乎正交（cosine ≈ 0），意味着两个 loss 的\n      梯度方向彼此独立。这排除了 \"gradient conflict\"（负 cosine）和\n      \"gradient alignment\"（正 cosine）两个假设。\n      关键原因：(1) occ head 输入是 2176d 拼接特征经 Linear(2176→256) 降维，\n      梯度回传到 2176d 空间后被稀释到高维中的一个低秩子空间；\n      (2) action loss 通过 LLM backbone 回传到 encoder，路径极长（7.65B params），\n      梯度信号经过大量非线性变换后失去方向性。\n      两条梯度路径在如此高维空间中自然正交——这是维度的诅咒，不是机制信号。\n      Gradient norms 也相似（0.079-0.085 范围），Detach（0.080）与 Vanilla（0.079）\n      几乎无差异，说明 occ loss 的额外梯度贡献微乎其微（occ norm 仅 0.031，\n      远小于 action norm 0.065）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Gradient Cosine Similarity (Encoder Layers)\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"cos(grad_action, grad_occ)\", \"grad_action_norm\", \"grad_occ_norm\", \"grad_total_norm\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Full OCC\", \"0.012 ± 0.038\", \"0.0654\", \"0.0312\", \"0.0847\"]\n          - [\"Random OCC\", \"-0.008 ± 0.042\", \"0.0641\", \"0.0298\", \"0.0823\"]\n          - [\"Detach\", \"N/A\", \"0.0654\", \"N/A (detached)\", \"0.0802\"]\n          - [\"Vanilla\", \"N/A (no aux)\", \"0.0654\", \"N/A (no aux head)\", \"0.0791\"]\n      - name: \"Per-Layer Gradient Cosine (Full OCC)\"\n        columns: [\"Layer\", \"DINOv2\", \"SigLIP\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Layer 8\", \"0.003\", \"0.025\"]\n          - [\"Layer 16\", \"0.018\", \"0.011\"]\n          - [\"Layer 24\", \"-0.007\", \"-0.015\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Per-layer gradient cosine heatmap：X 轴为 encoder 层（DINOv2 L1-L24,\n        SigLIP L1-L27），Y 轴为条件（Full OCC, Random）。颜色编码 cosine 值。\n        整个 heatmap 几乎全是中灰色（值 ≈ 0），偶有浅蓝/浅红色噪声。\n        右侧 colorbar 范围 [-0.1, 0.1]。标题注释 \"No systematic gradient\n        alignment or conflict detected\"。\n      - >\n        Gradient norm 条形图：4 条件 × 3 组分（action, occ, total）。\n        所有条件的 total norm 相似（0.079-0.085），occ norm 远小于 action norm\n        （~0.03 vs ~0.065）。Detach 和 Vanilla 的 total norm 几乎相同。\n    analysis: >\n      Gradient 分析是 worst 档的核心 null result。两个关键发现摧毁 mechanism paper：\n      (1) Action-occ 梯度正交 → 无 gradient diversity/conflict 信号 →\n      \"auxiliary gradient flow provides regularization through gradient diversity\"\n      假说不成立。\n      (2) Occ gradient norm (0.031) 远小于 action gradient norm (0.065) →\n      occ loss 对 encoder 更新的贡献仅约 4.6%（0.031/0.065 * λ衰减后更低）→\n      梯度流效应太弱，不太可能是性能差异的因果原因。\n      Reviewer 会说：\"如果 occ 梯度如此微弱且与 action 梯度正交，\n      那 gradient flow 怎么可能是保护因素？更可能的解释是 BN 在 eval 模式下\n      使用的 running stats 不同——这是一个 evaluation artifact，不是训练效应。\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_024: CKA Representation Analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"CKA 表征分析 — 所有条件高度相似\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_024\"\n    description: >\n      在 50K checkpoint 上计算 Full OCC / Random OCC / Detach / Vanilla / Depth\n      五个条件的 encoder 中间层表征的 CKA（Centered Kernel Alignment）。\n      测试 Hypothesis 1（feature preservation / representation divergence）。\n    expected_results:\n      cka_pairwise_spatial_layers:\n        detach_vs_vanilla: 0.952\n        fullocc_vs_vanilla: 0.971\n        random_vs_vanilla: 0.965\n        depth_vs_vanilla: 0.968\n        fullocc_vs_random: 0.978\n        fullocc_vs_detach: 0.948\n        random_vs_detach: 0.956\n        depth_vs_detach: 0.960\n      cka_per_layer:\n        dino_layer_4: {detach_vs_vanilla: 0.992, fullocc_vs_vanilla: 0.996}\n        dino_layer_8: {detach_vs_vanilla: 0.985, fullocc_vs_vanilla: 0.993}\n        dino_layer_16: {detach_vs_vanilla: 0.968, fullocc_vs_vanilla: 0.982}\n        dino_layer_24: {detach_vs_vanilla: 0.941, fullocc_vs_vanilla: 0.965}\n        siglip_layer_8: {detach_vs_vanilla: 0.978, fullocc_vs_vanilla: 0.988}\n        siglip_layer_16: {detach_vs_vanilla: 0.961, fullocc_vs_vanilla: 0.976}\n        siglip_layer_27: {detach_vs_vanilla: 0.938, fullocc_vs_vanilla: 0.958}\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 worst 档下，CKA 分析显示所有条件（包括 Detach）的表征高度相似（>0.93）。\n      Detach vs Vanilla 的 CKA 为 0.952——虽然是最低值，但仍然极高。\n      这表明 Detach 的 3.4pp CAR 退化不是因为 encoder 表征退化。\n      原因分析：LoRA rank=32（alpha=16, effective scaling 0.5）仅改变 encoder 的\n      一个低秩子空间；50K 步的 fine-tuning 相对 pretrained weights 的改动很小；\n      且 occ head 仅有 1.2M params（0.016% of total），其梯度对 encoder 的影响\n      微乎其微。所有条件的 encoder 本质上都是 \"frozen pretrained + tiny LoRA delta\"，\n      自然高度相似。\n      CKA 在深层（layer 24/27）略低是正常的——深层对 task-specific 微调更敏感。\n      但即使最深层 Detach vs Vanilla 的 CKA（0.938/0.941）也远高于\n      \"表征退化\" 的合理阈值（通常 <0.8）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"CKA Pairwise Matrix (Spatial Encoder Layers Mean)\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"Vanilla\", \"Full OCC\", \"Random\", \"Detach\", \"Depth\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Vanilla\", \"1.000\", \"0.971\", \"0.965\", \"0.952\", \"0.968\"]\n          - [\"Full OCC\", \"0.971\", \"1.000\", \"0.978\", \"0.948\", \"0.973\"]\n          - [\"Random\", \"0.965\", \"0.978\", \"1.000\", \"0.956\", \"0.969\"]\n          - [\"Detach\", \"0.952\", \"0.948\", \"0.956\", \"1.000\", \"0.960\"]\n          - [\"Depth\", \"0.968\", \"0.973\", \"0.969\", \"0.960\", \"1.000\"]\n      - name: \"CKA Per-Layer Trend (Detach vs Vanilla)\"\n        columns: [\"Encoder\", \"Layer\", \"CKA\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"DINOv2\", \"4\", \"0.992\", \"nearly identical\"]\n          - [\"DINOv2\", \"8\", \"0.985\", \"nearly identical\"]\n          - [\"DINOv2\", \"16\", \"0.968\", \"very similar\"]\n          - [\"DINOv2\", \"24\", \"0.941\", \"similar (slight divergence)\"]\n          - [\"SigLIP\", \"8\", \"0.978\", \"very similar\"]\n          - [\"SigLIP\", \"16\", \"0.961\", \"similar\"]\n          - [\"SigLIP\", \"27\", \"0.938\", \"similar (most divergent)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        5×5 CKA pairwise heatmap：颜色范围 [0.93, 1.00]。几乎全蓝（高相似度）。\n        对角线为 1.0。Detach 行/列略浅但仍在深蓝区间。视觉冲击力弱——\n        \"所有条件都一样\" 的结论一目了然。\n      - >\n        Per-layer CKA 折线图：X 轴为层深度，Y 轴为 CKA。5 条线（5 个条件 vs Vanilla）。\n        所有线从 ~0.995（浅层）缓慢下降到 ~0.94（深层），线间距极小（<0.03）。\n        底部注释：\"All representations remain highly aligned regardless of training condition.\"\n    analysis: >\n      CKA 分析彻底否定了 \"Detach 损害源于表征退化\" 假说。如果 gradient flow\n      通过改善 encoder 表征来提供保护，那么 Detach（无 gradient flow）的表征\n      应该显著不同。但 CKA > 0.93 说明表征几乎相同——Detach 的损害\n      不在表征层面，而在 inference pipeline 的其他环节。\n      结合 gradient cosine 分析（occ 梯度贡献微弱），最合理的解释是：\n      Detach 条件下 OccHead 的 BatchNorm 在 eval mode 使用 running_mean/running_var，\n      这些统计量是在 detached forward pass 中累积的——encoder 输出不受 occ loss 约束，\n      但 BN 仍然在 training mode 中追踪这些统计量。Eval 时 BN 的 normalize 操作\n      使用了这些不匹配的统计量，通过 occ head 的残余连接或 multi-task head 的\n      共享路径微妙地干扰了 action 预测。\n      这是一个 engineering bug，不是 \"gradient flow mechanism\"。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_025: Reverse Cutoff\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Reverse Cutoff — 晚期启用 OCC loss\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_025\"\n    description: >\n      前 35K 步仅训练 action loss（无 occ），从 35K 步开始启用 occ_loss。\n      与 Cutoff@35K（前 35K 有 occ，后 15K 无）构成 2×2 设计。\n    expected_results:\n      TSR: 0.892\n      CAR: 0.776\n      collisions: 112\n      total_episodes: 500\n      checkpoint_step: 50000\n      n_seeds: 1\n      per_task:\n        T0: {TSR: 0.98, CAR: 0.98}\n        T1: {TSR: 0.94, CAR: 0.92}\n        T2: {TSR: 0.98, CAR: 0.94}\n        T3: {TSR: 0.96, CAR: 0.46}\n        T4: {TSR: 0.86, CAR: 0.98}\n        T5: {TSR: 0.38, CAR: 0.06}\n        T6: {TSR: 0.96, CAR: 0.50}\n        T7: {TSR: 0.94, CAR: 0.96}\n        T8: {TSR: 0.94, CAR: 0.98}\n        T9: {TSR: 0.98, CAR: 0.98}\n      temporal_2x2_design:\n        early_only_35k: {CAR: 0.746, label: \"Cutoff@35K\"}\n        late_only_35k: {CAR: 0.776, label: \"Reverse Cutoff\"}\n        full_50k: {CAR: 0.797, label: \"Full OCC\"}\n        none: {CAR: 0.780, label: \"Vanilla\"}\n    result_rationale: >\n      Reverse cutoff 的 CAR（0.776）≈ Vanilla（0.780），几乎无差异。\n      在 worst 档下，这是 BN artifact 假说的又一印证：\n      Reverse cutoff 在 35K-50K 启用 occ loss，BN stats 从 35K 开始积累，\n      到 50K 时只有 15K 步的 stats 历史。由于 occ loss 使用指数衰减\n      w(t)=0.01×exp(-t/50000)，在 35K-50K 阶段 λ 已从 ~0.005 衰减到 ~0.004，\n      occ loss 的贡献极微小。因此 reverse cutoff ≈ Vanilla 是完全预期的——\n      不是因为 \"late gradient flow doesn't help\"，而是因为 occ loss 在这个阶段\n      已经衰减到接近零。\n      2×2 设计的结果：early_only (0.746) < none (0.780) ≈ late_only (0.776) < full (0.797)。\n      这不支持任何 temporal 叙事——early_only 差是因为 BN mismatch，\n      late_only ≈ none 是因为 occ loss 已衰减，full 最好是因为 BN stats\n      全程一致。所有差异都可用 BN 解释。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"2×2 Temporal Design 结果\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"OCC 0-35K\", \"OCC 35K-50K\", \"CAR\", \"TSR\", \"vs Vanilla\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Full OCC\", \"Yes\", \"Yes\", \"0.797\", \"0.894\", \"+1.7pp\"]\n          - [\"Cutoff@35K\", \"Yes\", \"No\", \"0.746\", \"0.864\", \"-3.4pp\"]\n          - [\"Reverse Cutoff\", \"No\", \"Yes\", \"0.776\", \"0.892\", \"-0.4pp\"]\n          - [\"Vanilla\", \"No\", \"No\", \"0.780\", \"0.907\", \"baseline\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        2×2 矩阵图：行为 \"Early OCC (0-35K)\" {Yes/No}，列为 \"Late OCC (35K-50K)\" {Yes/No}。\n        每个格子显示 CAR 值和置信区间。左下格（Cutoff@35K）最差且有大误差棒，\n        其余三格几乎相同（0.776-0.797）。注释：\"Only the early-then-stop condition\n        shows harm — consistent with BN stats mismatch, not gradient flow timing.\"\n    analysis: >\n      2×2 设计的结果是 BN artifact 解释的决定性证据。如果 gradient flow timing\n      是因果因素，应该看到：early > none（早期梯度流有保护效果）和\n      late > none（晚期梯度流也有效果）。但实际是：\n      early < none（因为 BN mismatch）和 late ≈ none（因为 occ loss 已衰减）。\n      Full = early + late > 单独任一，只是因为全程 BN stats 一致。\n      Reviewer 的 kill shot：\"Your 2×2 design actually demonstrates that the harm\n      comes from stopping OCC training (BN stats freeze) rather than from\n      gradient flow per se. The reverse cutoff is effectively a control that\n      shows occ_loss at late stages contributes nothing due to exponential decay.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_027: Detach + LayerNorm — 关键实验\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Detach + LayerNorm OccHead — BN Artifact 确认实验\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_027\"\n    description: >\n      将 OccHead 中的 BatchNorm2d 替换为 LayerNorm，在 Detach 模式下训练。\n      LayerNorm 不使用 running stats（每次 forward 现算），因此不存在\n      training-eval distribution shift。如果 Detach+LN 不再损害 → BN 是 confound。\n    expected_results:\n      TSR: 0.906\n      CAR: 0.782\n      collisions: 109\n      total_episodes: 500\n      checkpoint_step: 50000\n      n_seeds: 1\n      per_task:\n        T0: {TSR: 0.98, CAR: 0.98}\n        T1: {TSR: 0.96, CAR: 0.92}\n        T2: {TSR: 1.00, CAR: 0.94}\n        T3: {TSR: 0.98, CAR: 0.48}\n        T4: {TSR: 0.88, CAR: 0.98}\n        T5: {TSR: 0.42, CAR: 0.08}\n        T6: {TSR: 0.98, CAR: 0.56}\n        T7: {TSR: 0.94, CAR: 0.96}\n        T8: {TSR: 0.94, CAR: 1.00}\n        T9: {TSR: 0.98, CAR: 0.92}\n      comparison:\n        detach_bn_CAR: 0.746\n        detach_ln_CAR: 0.782\n        vanilla_CAR: 0.780\n        delta_detach_bn_vs_vanilla: \"-3.4pp\"\n        delta_detach_ln_vs_vanilla: \"+0.2pp\"\n        bn_artifact_contribution: \"100% (3.6pp out of 3.4pp gap eliminated)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 worst 档下，Detach+LayerNorm 的 CAR（0.782）≈ Vanilla（0.780）。\n      这直接证明 Detach 的 3.4pp 损害完全来自 BatchNorm running stats artifact，\n      而非 gradient flow 的缺失。\n      机制：BatchNorm2d 在 training mode 中使用 batch statistics，但在 eval mode 中\n      使用 running_mean 和 running_var（通过 exponential moving average 在训练中累积）。\n      Detach 模式下，occ head 接收 detached encoder features——这些特征的分布\n      与 encoder 在 action loss 下继续更新后的真实分布逐渐偏离。BN 的 running stats\n      反映的是 detached 分布，不是 eval 时的实际分布。这种 mismatch 通过 BN 的\n      normalize 操作传播到 occ head 输出。虽然 Detach 切断了从 occ 到 encoder 的梯度，\n      occ head 的 forward pass 仍然执行——如果 framework 实现中 occ head 的 forward\n      以任何方式影响 action prediction（即使只是通过共享的 memory/buffer），\n      BN 的异常统计量就会造成微妙的 interference。\n      LayerNorm 每次 forward 现算统计量（不依赖 running stats），因此免疫于\n      这种 distribution shift。Detach+LN ≈ Vanilla 证实了 BN artifact 是唯一原因。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"BN vs LN in Detach Mode\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"Norm Type\", \"Gradient Flow\", \"TSR\", \"CAR\", \"vs Vanilla\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Detach+BN\", \"BatchNorm2d\", \"No\", \"0.812±0.163\", \"0.746±0.002\", \"-3.4pp\"]\n          - [\"Detach+LN\", \"LayerNorm\", \"No\", \"0.906\", \"0.782\", \"+0.2pp\"]\n          - [\"Full OCC+BN\", \"BatchNorm2d\", \"Yes\", \"0.894±0.050\", \"0.797±0.032\", \"+1.7pp\"]\n          - [\"Vanilla\", \"N/A\", \"N/A\", \"0.907±0.009\", \"0.780±0.012\", \"baseline\"]\n      - name: \"Detach Per-Task Recovery (BN → LN)\"\n        columns: [\"Task\", \"Detach+BN CAR (3-seed)\", \"Detach+LN CAR\", \"Vanilla CAR (3-seed)\", \"Recovery?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"T3\", \"0.180\", \"0.48\", \"0.380\", \"Full recovery\"]\n          - [\"T5\", \"0.047\", \"0.08\", \"0.073\", \"Full recovery\"]\n          - [\"T6\", \"0.380\", \"0.56\", \"0.573\", \"Full recovery\"]\n          - [\"T7\", \"1.000\", \"0.96\", \"0.973\", \"No harm (both high)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Bar chart 核心图：4 组条形（Detach+BN, Detach+LN, Full OCC+BN, Vanilla）。\n        Y 轴 CAR。Detach+BN 明显低（0.746），其余三组几乎等高（0.78-0.80）。\n        从 Detach+BN 到 Detach+LN 画一个 arrow，标注 \"+3.6pp (BN artifact eliminated)\"。\n        这是 worst 档 paper 的 Figure 1 候选——直接展示 BN confound。\n      - >\n        Detach+BN vs Detach+LN per-task heatmap 对比：左右两个 10-task heatmap。\n        Detach+BN 的 T3/T5/T6 呈深色（低 CAR），Detach+LN 这些位置恢复到\n        Vanilla 水平。视觉上 \"Detach+LN 的 heatmap 和 Vanilla 几乎一样\"。\n    analysis: >\n      plan_027 是 worst 档的 \"fatal experiment\"。Detach+LN ≈ Vanilla 意味着：\n      (1) 核心 claim \"gradient flow is necessary\" 被完全消解——\n      gradient flow 不是保护因素，BN running stats 才是损害来源；\n      (2) 所有其他实验的解释需要重新审视——Full OCC \"不损害\" 不是因为\n      梯度流提供了正则化，而是因为有梯度流时 BN stats 与 encoder 保持一致；\n      (3) Random OCC ≈ Full OCC 不再说明 \"spatial content 无关\"，而是说明\n      \"只要 BN stats 一致，任何 aux task 都不会损害\"。\n      Paper 必须完全 reframe：从 \"gradient flow necessity\" 转向\n      \"BatchNorm pitfall in detached auxiliary heads\"。\n      新贡献变成：VLA 社区使用 auxiliary heads 时，如果 detach gradients，\n      必须避免 BatchNorm（用 LayerNorm/GroupNorm 替代），否则 eval-time\n      distribution shift 会损害性能。这是一个实用的 engineering insight，\n      但不是 mechanism-level scientific contribution。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_028: Second Benchmark (P2)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Second Benchmark — LIBERO-Object/Goal (P2, 大概率不跑)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_028\"\n    description: >\n      在 SafeLIBERO LIBERO-Object 或 LIBERO-Goal 上重复 5 条件实验。\n      78 GPU hours，P2 优先级，deadline 前大概率无法执行。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"NOT_RUN (P2 priority, 78 GPU hours, deadline constraint)\"\n      if_imagined:\n        libero_object_conditions:\n          vanilla_CAR: 0.812\n          fullocc_CAR: 0.808\n          random_CAR: 0.805\n          detach_bn_CAR: 0.798\n          detach_ln_CAR: 0.810\n        detach_delta: \"-1.4pp (much smaller than LIBERO-Spatial's -3.4pp)\"\n        detach_bn_vs_ln_delta: \"+1.2pp (smaller BN artifact on different tasks)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 worst 档下，即使跑了第二个 benchmark，结果也不支持泛化性：\n      (1) LIBERO-Object 的碰撞模式与 LIBERO-Spatial 不同（物体操作 vs 空间导航），\n      Detach 的损害可能更小（-1.4pp vs -3.4pp），因为碰撞检测的任务依赖性更强；\n      (2) BN artifact 效应依赖于具体的 occ head 架构和任务，在不同 benchmark\n      上表现不同，削弱了 \"general pitfall\" 的叙事；\n      (3) 78 GPU hours 的投入产出比极低——只是在第二个 benchmark 上重复了\n      \"BN artifact\" 的发现，没有新的 scientific insight。\n      不跑更好——在 Limitations 中承认 single-benchmark 是比实际跑一个\n      inconsistent 结果更安全的策略。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cross-Benchmark Consistency (Imagined)\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"Detach Δ CAR\", \"BN→LN Recovery\", \"Consistent?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LIBERO-Spatial\", \"-3.4pp\", \"+3.6pp (full)\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"LIBERO-Object (imagined)\", \"-1.4pp\", \"+1.2pp (partial)\", \"Partially\"]\n          - [\"Interpretation\", \"—\", \"—\", \"Effect size varies by task suite\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Cross-benchmark comparison bar chart（如果跑了）：\n        左组 LIBERO-Spatial，右组 LIBERO-Object，每组 5 条件。\n        LIBERO-Object 的条件间差异更小，Detach 退化不显著。\n        视觉上 \"第二个 benchmark 没有复现第一个的 pattern\"。\n    analysis: >\n      P2 优先级意味着在 CoRL deadline 前几乎不可能跑完。\n      在 worst 档下，这反而是好事——如果跑了且结果 inconsistent，\n      reviewer 会直接判定 findings 不泛化（RC4+RC5 叠加攻击）。\n      不跑的风险（single benchmark limitation）可以在 Limitations 中诚实承认，\n      reviewer 通常对诚实的 limitation 声明比对 inconsistent 数据更宽容。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Aggregated Worst-Tier Analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Worst-Tier 全局综合分析\"\n    plan_id: \"aggregate\"\n    description: >\n      综合所有 planned 实验在 worst 档下的联合含义，评估论文可行性和最优 framing。\n    expected_results:\n      core_claim_status: \"DISSOLVED — Detach harm fully attributed to BN artifact\"\n      mechanism_analysis_status: \"NULL — CKA and gradient cosine provide no mechanism signal\"\n      temporal_dynamics_status: \"ANOMALOUS — U-shaped dose-response contradicts gradient flow hypothesis\"\n      paper_viability: \"MARGINAL — needs complete reframe from mechanism to cautionary study\"\n      key_surviving_contributions:\n        C1_revised: \"BN running stats in detached auxiliary heads cause eval-time performance degradation in VLAs\"\n        C2_unchanged: \"5+ condition factorial study design methodology for VLA safety analysis\"\n        C3_revised: \"Spatial auxiliary supervision (BEV occ, depth) provides no safety benefit over no auxiliary (or random)\"\n      reviewer_attack_surface:\n        RC1_BN_artifact: \"FATAL if plan_027 confirms — entire gradient flow claim is a BN confound\"\n        RC4_single_VLA: \"MEDIUM — acknowledged limitation\"\n        RC5_single_benchmark: \"MEDIUM — acknowledged limitation\"\n        RC4_RC5_combined: \"HIGH — single VLA + single benchmark + BN artifact = n=1 engineering observation\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档的联合效应是毁灭性的。三条独立证据线同时指向 BN artifact：\n      (1) CKA 高相似度 → Detach 不改变表征 → 损害不在 encoder 层面；\n      (2) Gradient cosine ≈ 0 → 梯度流效应太弱 → 不是保护因素；\n      (3) Cutoff U 形曲线 → 中间截断最差 → BN mismatch 假说的预测。\n      加上 plan_027 的 kill shot（Detach+LN ≈ Vanilla），核心 claim 彻底崩溃。\n      但 paper 仍有价值——BN pitfall 本身是一个实用发现，VLA 社区\n      （RT-2, Octo, OpenVLA 等）广泛使用 auxiliary heads 但没人系统研究过\n      detach mode 下 normalization 层的行为。作为 cautionary study /\n      findings paper，仍可冲 CoRL，但需要：\n      (1) 极度精准的 writing，不 overclaim；\n      (2) 把 BN artifact 作为正面贡献而非尴尬的 confound；\n      (3) 强调方法论贡献（factorial design + SafeLIBERO 协议）；\n      (4) \"spatial content irrelevant\" 作为清晰的 negative finding。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Worst-Tier Evidence Summary\"\n        columns: [\"Evidence Line\", \"Result\", \"Implication for Core Claim\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"CKA Analysis\", \"All CKA > 0.93\", \"No representation divergence → harm not in encoder\"]\n          - [\"Gradient Cosine\", \"All cosine ≈ 0\", \"No gradient interaction → flow too weak to matter\"]\n          - [\"Cutoff Dose-Response\", \"U-shaped (non-monotonic)\", \"Contradicts gradient flow timing hypothesis\"]\n          - [\"2×2 Temporal Design\", \"Only early-stop harms\", \"Consistent with BN mismatch, not flow\"]\n          - [\"Detach+LayerNorm\", \"CAR ≈ Vanilla\", \"BN artifact confirmed as sole cause of Detach harm\"]\n          - [\"Multi-cutoff @15K\", \"Better than @35K\", \"Shorter exposure = less BN specialization = less mismatch\"]\n      - name: \"Revised Paper Contribution Structure (Worst Tier)\"\n        columns: [\"Contribution\", \"Content\", \"Strength\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"C1 (Main Finding)\", \"BatchNorm running stats in detached aux heads cause eval-time harm in VLAs\", \"Medium — engineering insight, not mechanism\"]\n          - [\"C2 (Negative Finding)\", \"Spatial auxiliary supervision provides no safety benefit for VLAs\", \"Medium-High — clear and actionable\"]\n          - [\"C3 (Methodology)\", \"5-condition factorial design + SafeLIBERO protocol for VLA safety evaluation\", \"Medium — reusable framework\"]\n          - [\"C4 (Practical Guidance)\", \"Use LayerNorm instead of BatchNorm in auxiliary heads if detaching gradients\", \"High — immediately actionable\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Paper overview figure (worst-tier version)：左半 5 条件 CAR bar chart，\n        右半 BN vs LN comparison。核心视觉信息从 \"gradient flow necessity\"\n        变为 \"BatchNorm pitfall\"。标注从 \"Detach harms due to no gradient flow\"\n        改为 \"Detach harms due to BN running stats mismatch (fixed by LayerNorm)\"。\n      - >\n        Mechanism analysis null result summary figure：3 panel——\n        (A) CKA heatmap（全蓝），(B) gradient cosine heatmap（全灰），\n        (C) dose-response U 形曲线。标题：\"Mechanism analysis reveals no gradient-level\n        or representation-level differences — harm traces to BatchNorm evaluation artifact.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst 档的论文仍然可以投 CoRL 2026，但定位必须从 mechanism paper 彻底转为\n      cautionary findings paper。核心价值不再是 \"why gradient flow matters\" 而是\n      \"what goes wrong when you detach auxiliary heads with BatchNorm in VLAs\"。\n      这是一个 niche 但有用的贡献——VLA fine-tuning 文献中缺乏对 auxiliary head\n      设计选择的系统分析，这篇论文填补了这个空白。\n      接受概率估计：30-40%（取决于 reviewer 是否认为 BN artifact 足够 novel、\n      是否接受 single VLA + single benchmark 的局限性、以及 writing 质量）。\n      关键风险：reviewer 可能认为 \"BatchNorm eval artifact\" 是已知问题\n      （BN 在 transfer learning 中的 pitfall 早有文献），在 VLA 上重复验证\n      不构成足够的 novelty。应对：强调 VLA-specific context（multi-modal encoder、\n      极大 backbone 上的 LoRA、指数衰减的 aux loss weight）使问题不 trivial。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8310,"cache_read_input_tokens":46790,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8310},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d969fedb-9e5c-4412-9cce-4b1a3a41528f","uuid":"c72c1dbe-9e85-46be-ae51-a81bc5b900d2"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":508121,"duration_api_ms":509813,"num_turns":8,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  核心 \"梯度流必要性\" claim 被 BatchNorm confound 消解。CKA 和 gradient cosine\n  分析均无机制信号——表征高度相似、梯度几乎正交。Cutoff 第 3 seed 崩溃导致巨大方差，\n  无法支撑 temporal 叙事。若跑 plan_027（Detach+LayerNorm），LayerNorm 版 Detach\n  不再损害，直接证实 BN running stats 是 confound。即使不跑 027，reviewer 也会提出\n  \"BN eval mode uses training running stats from detached forward passes\" 攻击，\n  作者无法反驳。新 framing 需完全放弃 mechanism paper 定位，转向\n  \"Hidden Pitfalls of Auxiliary Heads in VLA Fine-tuning: A Cautionary Study\"，\n  以 BN artifact 本身为贡献、5 条件 factorial 设计为方法论贡献、\n  \"spatial auxiliary supervision provides no safety benefit\" 为核心 negative finding。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_019: Cutoff seed 44 — RUNNING，需预测\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Cutoff s2 (seed 44) — 第 3 seed 崩溃\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_019\"\n    description: >\n      Cutoff@35K 第 3 seed。OCC loss 在 35K 步截断，之后仅训练 action loss。\n      在 worst 档下，该 seed 出现类似 detach_s2 的部分崩溃——\n      多个任务 TSR 大幅退化，拉低 3-seed 均值并放大方差。\n    expected_results:\n      TSR: 0.762\n      CAR: 0.672\n      collisions: 164\n      total_episodes: 500\n      checkpoint_step: 50000\n      per_task:\n        T0: {TSR: 0.96, CAR: 0.96}\n        T1: {TSR: 0.86, CAR: 0.86}\n        T2: {TSR: 0.94, CAR: 0.90}\n        T3: {TSR: 0.60, CAR: 0.08}\n        T4: {TSR: 0.38, CAR: 0.92}\n        T5: {TSR: 0.18, CAR: 0.02}\n        T6: {TSR: 0.88, CAR: 0.28}\n        T7: {TSR: 0.82, CAR: 0.88}\n        T8: {TSR: 0.90, CAR: 0.96}\n        T9: {TSR: 0.96, CAR: 0.86}\n      cutoff_3seed_aggregate:\n        seeds_used: [\"s0 (actual: 0.768)\", \"s1 (actual: 0.798)\", \"s2 (predicted: 0.672)\"]\n        mean_CAR: 0.746\n        mean_TSR: 0.864\n        std_CAR: 0.066\n        std_TSR: 0.088\n        vs_vanilla_CAR: \"-3.4pp\"\n        vs_fullocc_CAR: \"-5.1pp\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cutoff 在 35K 截断 OCC loss 后，occ head 的 BatchNorm 层 running stats 冻结在\n      35K 时刻的值。但 encoder 继续随 action loss 更新，导致 BN running stats 和后续\n      encoder 输出之间产生 distribution shift。这与 Detach 的 BN artifact 是同一机制的\n      变体——只是 Detach 是全程 stats 不匹配，Cutoff 是后半程不匹配。s2 种子恰好放大了\n      这一 distribution shift 的影响，T3/T4/T5 这些本身脆弱的任务首先崩溃。\n      3-seed 均值 CAR=0.746 落入 worst 档范围 [0.73, 0.76]，σ=0.066 > 0.040 阈值，\n      表明 Cutoff 条件的不稳定性与 Detach（TSR σ=0.163）是同一类问题的不同程度表现。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cutoff 3-seed 汇总 (含 s2 预测)\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"TSR\", \"CAR\", \"Collisions\", \"Status\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0 (seed 42)\", \"0.912\", \"0.768\", \"116\", \"actual\"]\n          - [\"s1 (seed 43)\", \"0.918\", \"0.798\", \"101\", \"actual\"]\n          - [\"s2 (seed 44)\", \"0.762\", \"0.672\", \"164\", \"predicted\"]\n          - [\"3-seed Mean\", \"0.864±0.088\", \"0.746±0.066\", \"127±33\", \"aggregate\"]\n      - name: \"Cutoff s2 per-task 崩溃模式\"\n        columns: [\"Task\", \"TSR\", \"CAR\", \"崩溃类型\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"T3\", \"0.60\", \"0.08\", \"CAR 系统性失败（同 Detach 模式）\"]\n          - [\"T4\", \"0.38\", \"0.92\", \"TSR 崩溃但 CAR 正常（策略退化）\"]\n          - [\"T5\", \"0.18\", \"0.02\", \"双重崩溃（最脆弱任务）\"]\n          - [\"T6\", \"0.88\", \"0.28\", \"CAR 退化\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Cutoff s2 per-task heatmap：10 个任务 × 2 指标（TSR/CAR），颜色编码。\n        T3/T4/T5/T6 区域呈现深色（低值），与 Detach s2 的崩溃模式高度相似。\n        右侧对比 Detach s2 的 heatmap，视觉上几乎重叠。\n    analysis: >\n      Cutoff s2 崩溃暴露了一个关键问题：截断 occ_loss 后 BN running stats 冻结，\n      但 encoder 继续更新，产生的 distribution shift 效应与 Detach 的 BN artifact\n      高度一致。这意味着 Cutoff 和 Detach 的损害可能共享同一根因（BN stats mismatch），\n      而非 \"gradient flow 缺失\"。Reviewer 会指出：如果 Cutoff 损害是因为 BN stats\n      过时而非梯度流消失，那么整个 temporal dynamics 叙事就是在测量 BN artifact\n      的时间演化，而非梯度流的因果效应。3-seed σ=0.066 也说明 Cutoff 条件不稳定，\n      单 seed 结果不可信，dose-response 实验（plan_020-022）的单 seed 设计更加脆弱。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_020 / plan_029: Multi-cutoff @15K\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Cutoff@15K — 极短梯度流暴露期\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: >\n      OCC loss 在 15K 步截断（仅占 50K 总训练的 30%）。\n      测试最短梯度流暴露期是否足以提供 \"保护\"。\n      plan_029 为同一实验的 P2 重复。\n    expected_results:\n      TSR: 0.872\n      CAR: 0.758\n      collisions: 121\n      total_episodes: 500\n      checkpoint_step: 50000\n      n_seeds: 1\n      per_task:\n        T0: {TSR: 0.98, CAR: 0.98}\n        T1: {TSR: 0.92, CAR: 0.90}\n        T2: {TSR: 0.98, CAR: 0.92}\n        T3: {TSR: 0.96, CAR: 0.36}\n        T4: {TSR: 0.82, CAR: 0.98}\n        T5: {TSR: 0.28, CAR: 0.06}\n        T6: {TSR: 0.96, CAR: 0.48}\n        T7: {TSR: 0.92, CAR: 0.96}\n        T8: {TSR: 0.92, CAR: 0.98}\n        T9: {TSR: 0.96, CAR: 0.96}\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 worst 档下，@15K 意外地比 @35K 3-seed 均值更好（0.758 vs 0.746）。\n      原因：15K 步时 BN running stats 刚刚开始积累，尚未深度耦合 encoder 输出分布；\n      截断后 BN stats 与后续 encoder 更新之间的 distribution shift 反而更小\n      （因为 stats 本身就不够 \"specialized\"，更接近初始化值）。\n      这是一个反直觉结果，直接破坏了 \"更长梯度流 → 更好保护\" 的 dose-response 假设。\n      Reviewer 会利用此结果论证：所谓的 \"gradient flow protection\" 其实就是\n      \"BN stats 与 encoder 的 distribution alignment\"——越短的暴露期，\n      BN stats 越接近通用初始化，反而越不会在截断后造成 mismatch。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Dose-Response 中间汇总 (@15K 定位)\"\n        columns: [\"Cutoff Point\", \"Seeds\", \"CAR\", \"vs Vanilla\", \"vs @35K\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"@15K\", \"1\", \"0.758\", \"-2.2pp\", \"+1.2pp\"]\n          - [\"@35K\", \"3\", \"0.746±0.066\", \"-3.4pp\", \"baseline\"]\n          - [\"Full (50K)\", \"3\", \"0.797±0.032\", \"+1.7pp\", \"+5.1pp\"]\n          - [\"Vanilla\", \"3\", \"0.780±0.012\", \"—\", \"+3.4pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Dose-response 折线图初步版本：X 轴为 cutoff step（15K, 35K, 50K），\n        Y 轴为 CAR。折线呈 V 形或非单调——@15K 高于 @35K——\n        与预期的单调递增 dose-response 相矛盾。\n        Vanilla 水平虚线作为参考。误差棒仅 @35K 有（3 seeds），其余为单 seed 点估计。\n    analysis: >\n      @15K 优于 @35K 的反直觉结果是 worst 档的关键证据。\n      这排除了 \"梯度流持续时间越长保护越强\" 的 dose-response 叙事。\n      单 seed 设计意味着这个数字本身不可信（seed variance 可达 ±5pp），\n      但即使重复 3 seeds，@15K 的 BN stats 与 encoder 的 mismatch\n      结构性地小于 @35K（因为 stats 更接近初始化），所以趋势大概率不变。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_021 / plan_026: Multi-cutoff @25K\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Cutoff@25K — 中间截断点\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_021\"\n    description: >\n      OCC loss 在 25K 步截断（50%训练进度）。plan_026 为同一实验。\n    expected_results:\n      TSR: 0.856\n      CAR: 0.742\n      collisions: 129\n      total_episodes: 500\n      checkpoint_step: 50000\n      n_seeds: 1\n      per_task:\n        T0: {TSR: 0.98, CAR: 0.96}\n        T1: {TSR: 0.90, CAR: 0.88}\n        T2: {TSR: 0.96, CAR: 0.90}\n        T3: {TSR: 0.92, CAR: 0.24}\n        T4: {TSR: 0.80, CAR: 0.96}\n        T5: {TSR: 0.24, CAR: 0.04}\n        T6: {TSR: 0.92, CAR: 0.38}\n        T7: {TSR: 0.88, CAR: 0.94}\n        T8: {TSR: 0.90, CAR: 0.98}\n        T9: {TSR: 0.96, CAR: 0.94}\n    result_rationale: >\n      @25K 的 CAR（0.742）比 @15K（0.758）更低，进一步强化非单调模式。\n      在 25K 步时 BN running stats 已经充分适应了有 occ gradient 的 encoder 分布；\n      截断后 encoder 继续 drift，BN stats 的 mismatch 比 @15K 更严重。\n      这是 BN artifact 假说的完美预测：暴露时间越长（但不到底），\n      BN stats 越 specialized，截断后的 mismatch 越大。\n      @15K（不够 specialized）和 Full 50K（无截断）都没有这个问题，\n      只有中间截断点（25K, 35K）最受影响。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Dose-Response 扩展 (加入 @25K)\"\n        columns: [\"Cutoff Point\", \"Seeds\", \"CAR\", \"Dose-Response 预期\", \"实际趋势\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"@15K\", \"1\", \"0.758\", \"最低（最短暴露）\", \"中等\"]\n          - [\"@25K\", \"1\", \"0.742\", \"中等\", \"最低\"]\n          - [\"@35K\", \"3\", \"0.746±0.066\", \"中-高\", \"中-低\"]\n          - [\"Full (50K)\", \"3\", \"0.797±0.032\", \"最高（最长暴露）\", \"最高\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Dose-response 折线图更新：X 轴 cutoff step（15K, 25K, 35K, 50K），\n        Y 轴 CAR。曲线呈 U 形——@25K 是最低点，@15K 和 50K 都较高。\n        这是 BN distribution shift 假说的直接预测（中间截断点 mismatch 最大），\n        与 gradient flow dose-response 假说（单调递增）完全矛盾。\n    analysis: >\n      @25K 产生的 U 形曲线是 BN artifact 解释的 smoking gun。\n      如果是 gradient flow 效应，应该单调递增；\n      如果是 BN stats mismatch，中间截断点应该最差（stats 足够 specialized\n      但训练又不完整），这正是观测到的模式。\n      然而，单 seed 设计使这个论证非常脆弱——\n      @15K 和 @25K 的差异（1.6pp）远在 seed variance 内。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_022 / plan_030: Multi-cutoff @45K\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Cutoff@45K — 近完整训练截断\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_022\"\n    description: >\n      OCC loss 在 45K 步截断（90% 训练进度）。plan_030 为同一实验。\n    expected_results:\n      TSR: 0.904\n      CAR: 0.774\n      collisions: 113\n      total_episodes: 500\n      checkpoint_step: 50000\n      n_seeds: 1\n      per_task:\n        T0: {TSR: 1.00, CAR: 0.98}\n        T1: {TSR: 0.94, CAR: 0.92}\n        T2: {TSR: 0.98, CAR: 0.94}\n        T3: {TSR: 0.98, CAR: 0.52}\n        T4: {TSR: 0.90, CAR: 0.98}\n        T5: {TSR: 0.36, CAR: 0.08}\n        T6: {TSR: 0.98, CAR: 0.52}\n        T7: {TSR: 0.94, CAR: 0.96}\n        T8: {TSR: 0.94, CAR: 0.98}\n        T9: {TSR: 0.98, CAR: 0.86}\n    result_rationale: >\n      @45K 接近完整训练（仅最后 5K 步无 occ loss），BN stats 与 encoder\n      几乎同步，截断后 drift 时间极短（5K 步），mismatch 很小。\n      CAR 0.774 接近 Vanilla（0.780），符合预期。\n      这不提供新信息——无论 gradient flow 假说还是 BN artifact 假说，\n      近完整训练截断都应该接近 Full OCC。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"完整 Dose-Response 曲线\"\n        columns: [\"Cutoff\", \"Seeds\", \"TSR\", \"CAR\", \"vs Vanilla CAR\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"@15K\", \"1\", \"0.872\", \"0.758\", \"-2.2pp\"]\n          - [\"@25K\", \"1\", \"0.856\", \"0.742\", \"-3.8pp\"]\n          - [\"@35K\", \"3\", \"0.864±0.088\", \"0.746±0.066\", \"-3.4pp\"]\n          - [\"@45K\", \"1\", \"0.904\", \"0.774\", \"-0.6pp\"]\n          - [\"Full @50K\", \"3\", \"0.894±0.050\", \"0.797±0.032\", \"+1.7pp\"]\n          - [\"Vanilla\", \"3\", \"0.907±0.009\", \"0.780±0.012\", \"baseline\"]\n          - [\"Detach\", \"3\", \"0.812±0.163\", \"0.746±0.002\", \"-3.4pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        完整 dose-response 图：X 轴为 cutoff step（15K→50K），Y 轴为 CAR。\n        曲线呈明显 U 形（@25K-35K 为谷底），而非预期的单调递增。\n        Vanilla 和 Detach 水平虚线标注。误差棒：仅 @35K（3 seeds）有 error bar，\n        其余为单点估计。一个注释框标出 \"BN mismatch window\" 解释 U 形成因。\n      - >\n        Violin plot 对比所有 7 条件（Vanilla, Full OCC, Random OCC, Detach,\n        Cutoff@15K/25K/35K/45K）的 CAR 分布，展示 cutoff 条件的高方差。\n    analysis: >\n      完整 dose-response 数据呈 U 形而非单调递增，与 gradient flow 假说矛盾，\n      与 BN stats mismatch 假说一致。但致命弱点：除 @35K 外均为单 seed，\n      任何结论都不具备统计效力。在 worst 档下，这些数据只能作为 \"suggestive\"\n      证据放在 appendix，无法支撑主文 claim。\n      对 paper 的影响：dose-response 从 \"strengthening evidence\" 降级为\n      \"exploratory analysis with inconclusive results\"。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_023: Gradient Norm + Cosine Analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Gradient Cosine & Norm Analysis — 无机制信号\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: >\n      在 50K checkpoint 上对 Full OCC / Random OCC / Detach / Vanilla 条件\n      执行 1-epoch forward+backward pass，记录 (1) action loss 和 occ loss\n      对 shared encoder 各层的梯度余弦相似度，(2) 各层梯度范数。\n      测试 Hypothesis 3（gradient diversity/conflict）。\n    expected_results:\n      gradient_cosine:\n        fullocc_action_vs_occ:\n          layer_mean: 0.012\n          layer_std: 0.038\n          range: [-0.04, 0.05]\n        random_action_vs_occ:\n          layer_mean: -0.008\n          layer_std: 0.042\n          range: [-0.05, 0.04]\n        detach_action_vs_occ: \"N/A (occ gradients detached, no encoder gradient)\"\n      gradient_norms:\n        fullocc_encoder_grad_norm: 0.0847\n        random_encoder_grad_norm: 0.0823\n        vanilla_encoder_grad_norm: 0.0791\n        detach_encoder_grad_norm: 0.0802\n        fullocc_action_grad_norm: 0.0654\n        fullocc_occ_grad_norm: 0.0312\n      per_layer_cosine_fullocc:\n        dino_layer_8: 0.003\n        dino_layer_16: 0.018\n        dino_layer_24: -0.007\n        siglip_layer_8: 0.025\n        siglip_layer_16: 0.011\n        siglip_layer_24: -0.015\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 worst 档下，gradient cosine 分析产生 null result。所有条件的 action 和\n      occ 梯度在 shared encoder 层几乎正交（cosine ≈ 0），意味着两个 loss 的\n      梯度方向彼此独立。这排除了 \"gradient conflict\"（负 cosine）和\n      \"gradient alignment\"（正 cosine）两个假设。\n      关键原因：(1) occ head 输入是 2176d 拼接特征经 Linear(2176→256) 降维，\n      梯度回传到 2176d 空间后被稀释到高维中的一个低秩子空间；\n      (2) action loss 通过 LLM backbone 回传到 encoder，路径极长（7.65B params），\n      梯度信号经过大量非线性变换后失去方向性。\n      两条梯度路径在如此高维空间中自然正交——这是维度的诅咒，不是机制信号。\n      Gradient norms 也相似（0.079-0.085 范围），Detach（0.080）与 Vanilla（0.079）\n      几乎无差异，说明 occ loss 的额外梯度贡献微乎其微（occ norm 仅 0.031，\n      远小于 action norm 0.065）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Gradient Cosine Similarity (Encoder Layers)\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"cos(grad_action, grad_occ)\", \"grad_action_norm\", \"grad_occ_norm\", \"grad_total_norm\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Full OCC\", \"0.012 ± 0.038\", \"0.0654\", \"0.0312\", \"0.0847\"]\n          - [\"Random OCC\", \"-0.008 ± 0.042\", \"0.0641\", \"0.0298\", \"0.0823\"]\n          - [\"Detach\", \"N/A\", \"0.0654\", \"N/A (detached)\", \"0.0802\"]\n          - [\"Vanilla\", \"N/A (no aux)\", \"0.0654\", \"N/A (no aux head)\", \"0.0791\"]\n      - name: \"Per-Layer Gradient Cosine (Full OCC)\"\n        columns: [\"Layer\", \"DINOv2\", \"SigLIP\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Layer 8\", \"0.003\", \"0.025\"]\n          - [\"Layer 16\", \"0.018\", \"0.011\"]\n          - [\"Layer 24\", \"-0.007\", \"-0.015\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Per-layer gradient cosine heatmap：X 轴为 encoder 层（DINOv2 L1-L24,\n        SigLIP L1-L27），Y 轴为条件（Full OCC, Random）。颜色编码 cosine 值。\n        整个 heatmap 几乎全是中灰色（值 ≈ 0），偶有浅蓝/浅红色噪声。\n        右侧 colorbar 范围 [-0.1, 0.1]。标题注释 \"No systematic gradient\n        alignment or conflict detected\"。\n      - >\n        Gradient norm 条形图：4 条件 × 3 组分（action, occ, total）。\n        所有条件的 total norm 相似（0.079-0.085），occ norm 远小于 action norm\n        （~0.03 vs ~0.065）。Detach 和 Vanilla 的 total norm 几乎相同。\n    analysis: >\n      Gradient 分析是 worst 档的核心 null result。两个关键发现摧毁 mechanism paper：\n      (1) Action-occ 梯度正交 → 无 gradient diversity/conflict 信号 →\n      \"auxiliary gradient flow provides regularization through gradient diversity\"\n      假说不成立。\n      (2) Occ gradient norm (0.031) 远小于 action gradient norm (0.065) →\n      occ loss 对 encoder 更新的贡献仅约 4.6%（0.031/0.065 * λ衰减后更低）→\n      梯度流效应太弱，不太可能是性能差异的因果原因。\n      Reviewer 会说：\"如果 occ 梯度如此微弱且与 action 梯度正交，\n      那 gradient flow 怎么可能是保护因素？更可能的解释是 BN 在 eval 模式下\n      使用的 running stats 不同——这是一个 evaluation artifact，不是训练效应。\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_024: CKA Representation Analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"CKA 表征分析 — 所有条件高度相似\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_024\"\n    description: >\n      在 50K checkpoint 上计算 Full OCC / Random OCC / Detach / Vanilla / Depth\n      五个条件的 encoder 中间层表征的 CKA（Centered Kernel Alignment）。\n      测试 Hypothesis 1（feature preservation / representation divergence）。\n    expected_results:\n      cka_pairwise_spatial_layers:\n        detach_vs_vanilla: 0.952\n        fullocc_vs_vanilla: 0.971\n        random_vs_vanilla: 0.965\n        depth_vs_vanilla: 0.968\n        fullocc_vs_random: 0.978\n        fullocc_vs_detach: 0.948\n        random_vs_detach: 0.956\n        depth_vs_detach: 0.960\n      cka_per_layer:\n        dino_layer_4: {detach_vs_vanilla: 0.992, fullocc_vs_vanilla: 0.996}\n        dino_layer_8: {detach_vs_vanilla: 0.985, fullocc_vs_vanilla: 0.993}\n        dino_layer_16: {detach_vs_vanilla: 0.968, fullocc_vs_vanilla: 0.982}\n        dino_layer_24: {detach_vs_vanilla: 0.941, fullocc_vs_vanilla: 0.965}\n        siglip_layer_8: {detach_vs_vanilla: 0.978, fullocc_vs_vanilla: 0.988}\n        siglip_layer_16: {detach_vs_vanilla: 0.961, fullocc_vs_vanilla: 0.976}\n        siglip_layer_27: {detach_vs_vanilla: 0.938, fullocc_vs_vanilla: 0.958}\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 worst 档下，CKA 分析显示所有条件（包括 Detach）的表征高度相似（>0.93）。\n      Detach vs Vanilla 的 CKA 为 0.952——虽然是最低值，但仍然极高。\n      这表明 Detach 的 3.4pp CAR 退化不是因为 encoder 表征退化。\n      原因分析：LoRA rank=32（alpha=16, effective scaling 0.5）仅改变 encoder 的\n      一个低秩子空间；50K 步的 fine-tuning 相对 pretrained weights 的改动很小；\n      且 occ head 仅有 1.2M params（0.016% of total），其梯度对 encoder 的影响\n      微乎其微。所有条件的 encoder 本质上都是 \"frozen pretrained + tiny LoRA delta\"，\n      自然高度相似。\n      CKA 在深层（layer 24/27）略低是正常的——深层对 task-specific 微调更敏感。\n      但即使最深层 Detach vs Vanilla 的 CKA（0.938/0.941）也远高于\n      \"表征退化\" 的合理阈值（通常 <0.8）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"CKA Pairwise Matrix (Spatial Encoder Layers Mean)\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"Vanilla\", \"Full OCC\", \"Random\", \"Detach\", \"Depth\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Vanilla\", \"1.000\", \"0.971\", \"0.965\", \"0.952\", \"0.968\"]\n          - [\"Full OCC\", \"0.971\", \"1.000\", \"0.978\", \"0.948\", \"0.973\"]\n          - [\"Random\", \"0.965\", \"0.978\", \"1.000\", \"0.956\", \"0.969\"]\n          - [\"Detach\", \"0.952\", \"0.948\", \"0.956\", \"1.000\", \"0.960\"]\n          - [\"Depth\", \"0.968\", \"0.973\", \"0.969\", \"0.960\", \"1.000\"]\n      - name: \"CKA Per-Layer Trend (Detach vs Vanilla)\"\n        columns: [\"Encoder\", \"Layer\", \"CKA\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"DINOv2\", \"4\", \"0.992\", \"nearly identical\"]\n          - [\"DINOv2\", \"8\", \"0.985\", \"nearly identical\"]\n          - [\"DINOv2\", \"16\", \"0.968\", \"very similar\"]\n          - [\"DINOv2\", \"24\", \"0.941\", \"similar (slight divergence)\"]\n          - [\"SigLIP\", \"8\", \"0.978\", \"very similar\"]\n          - [\"SigLIP\", \"16\", \"0.961\", \"similar\"]\n          - [\"SigLIP\", \"27\", \"0.938\", \"similar (most divergent)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        5×5 CKA pairwise heatmap：颜色范围 [0.93, 1.00]。几乎全蓝（高相似度）。\n        对角线为 1.0。Detach 行/列略浅但仍在深蓝区间。视觉冲击力弱——\n        \"所有条件都一样\" 的结论一目了然。\n      - >\n        Per-layer CKA 折线图：X 轴为层深度，Y 轴为 CKA。5 条线（5 个条件 vs Vanilla）。\n        所有线从 ~0.995（浅层）缓慢下降到 ~0.94（深层），线间距极小（<0.03）。\n        底部注释：\"All representations remain highly aligned regardless of training condition.\"\n    analysis: >\n      CKA 分析彻底否定了 \"Detach 损害源于表征退化\" 假说。如果 gradient flow\n      通过改善 encoder 表征来提供保护，那么 Detach（无 gradient flow）的表征\n      应该显著不同。但 CKA > 0.93 说明表征几乎相同——Detach 的损害\n      不在表征层面，而在 inference pipeline 的其他环节。\n      结合 gradient cosine 分析（occ 梯度贡献微弱），最合理的解释是：\n      Detach 条件下 OccHead 的 BatchNorm 在 eval mode 使用 running_mean/running_var，\n      这些统计量是在 detached forward pass 中累积的——encoder 输出不受 occ loss 约束，\n      但 BN 仍然在 training mode 中追踪这些统计量。Eval 时 BN 的 normalize 操作\n      使用了这些不匹配的统计量，通过 occ head 的残余连接或 multi-task head 的\n      共享路径微妙地干扰了 action 预测。\n      这是一个 engineering bug，不是 \"gradient flow mechanism\"。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_025: Reverse Cutoff\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Reverse Cutoff — 晚期启用 OCC loss\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_025\"\n    description: >\n      前 35K 步仅训练 action loss（无 occ），从 35K 步开始启用 occ_loss。\n      与 Cutoff@35K（前 35K 有 occ，后 15K 无）构成 2×2 设计。\n    expected_results:\n      TSR: 0.892\n      CAR: 0.776\n      collisions: 112\n      total_episodes: 500\n      checkpoint_step: 50000\n      n_seeds: 1\n      per_task:\n        T0: {TSR: 0.98, CAR: 0.98}\n        T1: {TSR: 0.94, CAR: 0.92}\n        T2: {TSR: 0.98, CAR: 0.94}\n        T3: {TSR: 0.96, CAR: 0.46}\n        T4: {TSR: 0.86, CAR: 0.98}\n        T5: {TSR: 0.38, CAR: 0.06}\n        T6: {TSR: 0.96, CAR: 0.50}\n        T7: {TSR: 0.94, CAR: 0.96}\n        T8: {TSR: 0.94, CAR: 0.98}\n        T9: {TSR: 0.98, CAR: 0.98}\n      temporal_2x2_design:\n        early_only_35k: {CAR: 0.746, label: \"Cutoff@35K\"}\n        late_only_35k: {CAR: 0.776, label: \"Reverse Cutoff\"}\n        full_50k: {CAR: 0.797, label: \"Full OCC\"}\n        none: {CAR: 0.780, label: \"Vanilla\"}\n    result_rationale: >\n      Reverse cutoff 的 CAR（0.776）≈ Vanilla（0.780），几乎无差异。\n      在 worst 档下，这是 BN artifact 假说的又一印证：\n      Reverse cutoff 在 35K-50K 启用 occ loss，BN stats 从 35K 开始积累，\n      到 50K 时只有 15K 步的 stats 历史。由于 occ loss 使用指数衰减\n      w(t)=0.01×exp(-t/50000)，在 35K-50K 阶段 λ 已从 ~0.005 衰减到 ~0.004，\n      occ loss 的贡献极微小。因此 reverse cutoff ≈ Vanilla 是完全预期的——\n      不是因为 \"late gradient flow doesn't help\"，而是因为 occ loss 在这个阶段\n      已经衰减到接近零。\n      2×2 设计的结果：early_only (0.746) < none (0.780) ≈ late_only (0.776) < full (0.797)。\n      这不支持任何 temporal 叙事——early_only 差是因为 BN mismatch，\n      late_only ≈ none 是因为 occ loss 已衰减，full 最好是因为 BN stats\n      全程一致。所有差异都可用 BN 解释。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"2×2 Temporal Design 结果\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"OCC 0-35K\", \"OCC 35K-50K\", \"CAR\", \"TSR\", \"vs Vanilla\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Full OCC\", \"Yes\", \"Yes\", \"0.797\", \"0.894\", \"+1.7pp\"]\n          - [\"Cutoff@35K\", \"Yes\", \"No\", \"0.746\", \"0.864\", \"-3.4pp\"]\n          - [\"Reverse Cutoff\", \"No\", \"Yes\", \"0.776\", \"0.892\", \"-0.4pp\"]\n          - [\"Vanilla\", \"No\", \"No\", \"0.780\", \"0.907\", \"baseline\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        2×2 矩阵图：行为 \"Early OCC (0-35K)\" {Yes/No}，列为 \"Late OCC (35K-50K)\" {Yes/No}。\n        每个格子显示 CAR 值和置信区间。左下格（Cutoff@35K）最差且有大误差棒，\n        其余三格几乎相同（0.776-0.797）。注释：\"Only the early-then-stop condition\n        shows harm — consistent with BN stats mismatch, not gradient flow timing.\"\n    analysis: >\n      2×2 设计的结果是 BN artifact 解释的决定性证据。如果 gradient flow timing\n      是因果因素，应该看到：early > none（早期梯度流有保护效果）和\n      late > none（晚期梯度流也有效果）。但实际是：\n      early < none（因为 BN mismatch）和 late ≈ none（因为 occ loss 已衰减）。\n      Full = early + late > 单独任一，只是因为全程 BN stats 一致。\n      Reviewer 的 kill shot：\"Your 2×2 design actually demonstrates that the harm\n      comes from stopping OCC training (BN stats freeze) rather than from\n      gradient flow per se. The reverse cutoff is effectively a control that\n      shows occ_loss at late stages contributes nothing due to exponential decay.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_027: Detach + LayerNorm — 关键实验\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Detach + LayerNorm OccHead — BN Artifact 确认实验\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_027\"\n    description: >\n      将 OccHead 中的 BatchNorm2d 替换为 LayerNorm，在 Detach 模式下训练。\n      LayerNorm 不使用 running stats（每次 forward 现算），因此不存在\n      training-eval distribution shift。如果 Detach+LN 不再损害 → BN 是 confound。\n    expected_results:\n      TSR: 0.906\n      CAR: 0.782\n      collisions: 109\n      total_episodes: 500\n      checkpoint_step: 50000\n      n_seeds: 1\n      per_task:\n        T0: {TSR: 0.98, CAR: 0.98}\n        T1: {TSR: 0.96, CAR: 0.92}\n        T2: {TSR: 1.00, CAR: 0.94}\n        T3: {TSR: 0.98, CAR: 0.48}\n        T4: {TSR: 0.88, CAR: 0.98}\n        T5: {TSR: 0.42, CAR: 0.08}\n        T6: {TSR: 0.98, CAR: 0.56}\n        T7: {TSR: 0.94, CAR: 0.96}\n        T8: {TSR: 0.94, CAR: 1.00}\n        T9: {TSR: 0.98, CAR: 0.92}\n      comparison:\n        detach_bn_CAR: 0.746\n        detach_ln_CAR: 0.782\n        vanilla_CAR: 0.780\n        delta_detach_bn_vs_vanilla: \"-3.4pp\"\n        delta_detach_ln_vs_vanilla: \"+0.2pp\"\n        bn_artifact_contribution: \"100% (3.6pp out of 3.4pp gap eliminated)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 worst 档下，Detach+LayerNorm 的 CAR（0.782）≈ Vanilla（0.780）。\n      这直接证明 Detach 的 3.4pp 损害完全来自 BatchNorm running stats artifact，\n      而非 gradient flow 的缺失。\n      机制：BatchNorm2d 在 training mode 中使用 batch statistics，但在 eval mode 中\n      使用 running_mean 和 running_var（通过 exponential moving average 在训练中累积）。\n      Detach 模式下，occ head 接收 detached encoder features——这些特征的分布\n      与 encoder 在 action loss 下继续更新后的真实分布逐渐偏离。BN 的 running stats\n      反映的是 detached 分布，不是 eval 时的实际分布。这种 mismatch 通过 BN 的\n      normalize 操作传播到 occ head 输出。虽然 Detach 切断了从 occ 到 encoder 的梯度，\n      occ head 的 forward pass 仍然执行——如果 framework 实现中 occ head 的 forward\n      以任何方式影响 action prediction（即使只是通过共享的 memory/buffer），\n      BN 的异常统计量就会造成微妙的 interference。\n      LayerNorm 每次 forward 现算统计量（不依赖 running stats），因此免疫于\n      这种 distribution shift。Detach+LN ≈ Vanilla 证实了 BN artifact 是唯一原因。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"BN vs LN in Detach Mode\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"Norm Type\", \"Gradient Flow\", \"TSR\", \"CAR\", \"vs Vanilla\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Detach+BN\", \"BatchNorm2d\", \"No\", \"0.812±0.163\", \"0.746±0.002\", \"-3.4pp\"]\n          - [\"Detach+LN\", \"LayerNorm\", \"No\", \"0.906\", \"0.782\", \"+0.2pp\"]\n          - [\"Full OCC+BN\", \"BatchNorm2d\", \"Yes\", \"0.894±0.050\", \"0.797±0.032\", \"+1.7pp\"]\n          - [\"Vanilla\", \"N/A\", \"N/A\", \"0.907±0.009\", \"0.780±0.012\", \"baseline\"]\n      - name: \"Detach Per-Task Recovery (BN → LN)\"\n        columns: [\"Task\", \"Detach+BN CAR (3-seed)\", \"Detach+LN CAR\", \"Vanilla CAR (3-seed)\", \"Recovery?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"T3\", \"0.180\", \"0.48\", \"0.380\", \"Full recovery\"]\n          - [\"T5\", \"0.047\", \"0.08\", \"0.073\", \"Full recovery\"]\n          - [\"T6\", \"0.380\", \"0.56\", \"0.573\", \"Full recovery\"]\n          - [\"T7\", \"1.000\", \"0.96\", \"0.973\", \"No harm (both high)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Bar chart 核心图：4 组条形（Detach+BN, Detach+LN, Full OCC+BN, Vanilla）。\n        Y 轴 CAR。Detach+BN 明显低（0.746），其余三组几乎等高（0.78-0.80）。\n        从 Detach+BN 到 Detach+LN 画一个 arrow，标注 \"+3.6pp (BN artifact eliminated)\"。\n        这是 worst 档 paper 的 Figure 1 候选——直接展示 BN confound。\n      - >\n        Detach+BN vs Detach+LN per-task heatmap 对比：左右两个 10-task heatmap。\n        Detach+BN 的 T3/T5/T6 呈深色（低 CAR），Detach+LN 这些位置恢复到\n        Vanilla 水平。视觉上 \"Detach+LN 的 heatmap 和 Vanilla 几乎一样\"。\n    analysis: >\n      plan_027 是 worst 档的 \"fatal experiment\"。Detach+LN ≈ Vanilla 意味着：\n      (1) 核心 claim \"gradient flow is necessary\" 被完全消解——\n      gradient flow 不是保护因素，BN running stats 才是损害来源；\n      (2) 所有其他实验的解释需要重新审视——Full OCC \"不损害\" 不是因为\n      梯度流提供了正则化，而是因为有梯度流时 BN stats 与 encoder 保持一致；\n      (3) Random OCC ≈ Full OCC 不再说明 \"spatial content 无关\"，而是说明\n      \"只要 BN stats 一致，任何 aux task 都不会损害\"。\n      Paper 必须完全 reframe：从 \"gradient flow necessity\" 转向\n      \"BatchNorm pitfall in detached auxiliary heads\"。\n      新贡献变成：VLA 社区使用 auxiliary heads 时，如果 detach gradients，\n      必须避免 BatchNorm（用 LayerNorm/GroupNorm 替代），否则 eval-time\n      distribution shift 会损害性能。这是一个实用的 engineering insight，\n      但不是 mechanism-level scientific contribution。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_028: Second Benchmark (P2)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Second Benchmark — LIBERO-Object/Goal (P2, 大概率不跑)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_028\"\n    description: >\n      在 SafeLIBERO LIBERO-Object 或 LIBERO-Goal 上重复 5 条件实验。\n      78 GPU hours，P2 优先级，deadline 前大概率无法执行。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"NOT_RUN (P2 priority, 78 GPU hours, deadline constraint)\"\n      if_imagined:\n        libero_object_conditions:\n          vanilla_CAR: 0.812\n          fullocc_CAR: 0.808\n          random_CAR: 0.805\n          detach_bn_CAR: 0.798\n          detach_ln_CAR: 0.810\n        detach_delta: \"-1.4pp (much smaller than LIBERO-Spatial's -3.4pp)\"\n        detach_bn_vs_ln_delta: \"+1.2pp (smaller BN artifact on different tasks)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 worst 档下，即使跑了第二个 benchmark，结果也不支持泛化性：\n      (1) LIBERO-Object 的碰撞模式与 LIBERO-Spatial 不同（物体操作 vs 空间导航），\n      Detach 的损害可能更小（-1.4pp vs -3.4pp），因为碰撞检测的任务依赖性更强；\n      (2) BN artifact 效应依赖于具体的 occ head 架构和任务，在不同 benchmark\n      上表现不同，削弱了 \"general pitfall\" 的叙事；\n      (3) 78 GPU hours 的投入产出比极低——只是在第二个 benchmark 上重复了\n      \"BN artifact\" 的发现，没有新的 scientific insight。\n      不跑更好——在 Limitations 中承认 single-benchmark 是比实际跑一个\n      inconsistent 结果更安全的策略。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cross-Benchmark Consistency (Imagined)\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"Detach Δ CAR\", \"BN→LN Recovery\", \"Consistent?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LIBERO-Spatial\", \"-3.4pp\", \"+3.6pp (full)\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"LIBERO-Object (imagined)\", \"-1.4pp\", \"+1.2pp (partial)\", \"Partially\"]\n          - [\"Interpretation\", \"—\", \"—\", \"Effect size varies by task suite\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Cross-benchmark comparison bar chart（如果跑了）：\n        左组 LIBERO-Spatial，右组 LIBERO-Object，每组 5 条件。\n        LIBERO-Object 的条件间差异更小，Detach 退化不显著。\n        视觉上 \"第二个 benchmark 没有复现第一个的 pattern\"。\n    analysis: >\n      P2 优先级意味着在 CoRL deadline 前几乎不可能跑完。\n      在 worst 档下，这反而是好事——如果跑了且结果 inconsistent，\n      reviewer 会直接判定 findings 不泛化（RC4+RC5 叠加攻击）。\n      不跑的风险（single benchmark limitation）可以在 Limitations 中诚实承认，\n      reviewer 通常对诚实的 limitation 声明比对 inconsistent 数据更宽容。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Aggregated Worst-Tier Analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Worst-Tier 全局综合分析\"\n    plan_id: \"aggregate\"\n    description: >\n      综合所有 planned 实验在 worst 档下的联合含义，评估论文可行性和最优 framing。\n    expected_results:\n      core_claim_status: \"DISSOLVED — Detach harm fully attributed to BN artifact\"\n      mechanism_analysis_status: \"NULL — CKA and gradient cosine provide no mechanism signal\"\n      temporal_dynamics_status: \"ANOMALOUS — U-shaped dose-response contradicts gradient flow hypothesis\"\n      paper_viability: \"MARGINAL — needs complete reframe from mechanism to cautionary study\"\n      key_surviving_contributions:\n        C1_revised: \"BN running stats in detached auxiliary heads cause eval-time performance degradation in VLAs\"\n        C2_unchanged: \"5+ condition factorial study design methodology for VLA safety analysis\"\n        C3_revised: \"Spatial auxiliary supervision (BEV occ, depth) provides no safety benefit over no auxiliary (or random)\"\n      reviewer_attack_surface:\n        RC1_BN_artifact: \"FATAL if plan_027 confirms — entire gradient flow claim is a BN confound\"\n        RC4_single_VLA: \"MEDIUM — acknowledged limitation\"\n        RC5_single_benchmark: \"MEDIUM — acknowledged limitation\"\n        RC4_RC5_combined: \"HIGH — single VLA + single benchmark + BN artifact = n=1 engineering observation\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档的联合效应是毁灭性的。三条独立证据线同时指向 BN artifact：\n      (1) CKA 高相似度 → Detach 不改变表征 → 损害不在 encoder 层面；\n      (2) Gradient cosine ≈ 0 → 梯度流效应太弱 → 不是保护因素；\n      (3) Cutoff U 形曲线 → 中间截断最差 → BN mismatch 假说的预测。\n      加上 plan_027 的 kill shot（Detach+LN ≈ Vanilla），核心 claim 彻底崩溃。\n      但 paper 仍有价值——BN pitfall 本身是一个实用发现，VLA 社区\n      （RT-2, Octo, OpenVLA 等）广泛使用 auxiliary heads 但没人系统研究过\n      detach mode 下 normalization 层的行为。作为 cautionary study /\n      findings paper，仍可冲 CoRL，但需要：\n      (1) 极度精准的 writing，不 overclaim；\n      (2) 把 BN artifact 作为正面贡献而非尴尬的 confound；\n      (3) 强调方法论贡献（factorial design + SafeLIBERO 协议）；\n      (4) \"spatial content irrelevant\" 作为清晰的 negative finding。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Worst-Tier Evidence Summary\"\n        columns: [\"Evidence Line\", \"Result\", \"Implication for Core Claim\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"CKA Analysis\", \"All CKA > 0.93\", \"No representation divergence → harm not in encoder\"]\n          - [\"Gradient Cosine\", \"All cosine ≈ 0\", \"No gradient interaction → flow too weak to matter\"]\n          - [\"Cutoff Dose-Response\", \"U-shaped (non-monotonic)\", \"Contradicts gradient flow timing hypothesis\"]\n          - [\"2×2 Temporal Design\", \"Only early-stop harms\", \"Consistent with BN mismatch, not flow\"]\n          - [\"Detach+LayerNorm\", \"CAR ≈ Vanilla\", \"BN artifact confirmed as sole cause of Detach harm\"]\n          - [\"Multi-cutoff @15K\", \"Better than @35K\", \"Shorter exposure = less BN specialization = less mismatch\"]\n      - name: \"Revised Paper Contribution Structure (Worst Tier)\"\n        columns: [\"Contribution\", \"Content\", \"Strength\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"C1 (Main Finding)\", \"BatchNorm running stats in detached aux heads cause eval-time harm in VLAs\", \"Medium — engineering insight, not mechanism\"]\n          - [\"C2 (Negative Finding)\", \"Spatial auxiliary supervision provides no safety benefit for VLAs\", \"Medium-High — clear and actionable\"]\n          - [\"C3 (Methodology)\", \"5-condition factorial design + SafeLIBERO protocol for VLA safety evaluation\", \"Medium — reusable framework\"]\n          - [\"C4 (Practical Guidance)\", \"Use LayerNorm instead of BatchNorm in auxiliary heads if detaching gradients\", \"High — immediately actionable\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Paper overview figure (worst-tier version)：左半 5 条件 CAR bar chart，\n        右半 BN vs LN comparison。核心视觉信息从 \"gradient flow necessity\"\n        变为 \"BatchNorm pitfall\"。标注从 \"Detach harms due to no gradient flow\"\n        改为 \"Detach harms due to BN running stats mismatch (fixed by LayerNorm)\"。\n      - >\n        Mechanism analysis null result summary figure：3 panel——\n        (A) CKA heatmap（全蓝），(B) gradient cosine heatmap（全灰），\n        (C) dose-response U 形曲线。标题：\"Mechanism analysis reveals no gradient-level\n        or representation-level differences — harm traces to BatchNorm evaluation artifact.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst 档的论文仍然可以投 CoRL 2026，但定位必须从 mechanism paper 彻底转为\n      cautionary findings paper。核心价值不再是 \"why gradient flow matters\" 而是\n      \"what goes wrong when you detach auxiliary heads with BatchNorm in VLAs\"。\n      这是一个 niche 但有用的贡献——VLA fine-tuning 文献中缺乏对 auxiliary head\n      设计选择的系统分析，这篇论文填补了这个空白。\n      接受概率估计：30-40%（取决于 reviewer 是否认为 BN artifact 足够 novel、\n      是否接受 single VLA + single benchmark 的局限性、以及 writing 质量）。\n      关键风险：reviewer 可能认为 \"BatchNorm eval artifact\" 是已知问题\n      （BN 在 transfer learning 中的 pitfall 早有文献），在 VLA 上重复验证\n      不构成足够的 novelty。应对：强调 VLA-specific context（multi-modal encoder、\n      极大 backbone 上的 LoRA、指数衰减的 aux loss weight）使问题不 trivial。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d969fedb-9e5c-4412-9cce-4b1a3a41528f","total_cost_usd":1.06411425,"usage":{"input_tokens":2880,"cache_creation_input_tokens":43259,"cache_read_input_tokens":183481,"output_tokens":26551,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":43259,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":26009,"cache_read_input_tokens":46790,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8310,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8310},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":23715,"outputTokens":23,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.02383,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2880,"outputTokens":26551,"cacheReadInputTokens":183481,"cacheCreationInputTokens":43259,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.04028425,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"daf66aab-89a2-4991-922b-a05f69493140"}
